WEBVTT


00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:06.700
In this video, we'll be completing our one
piece mitered neck band for a square neck

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.000
line.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:13.630
We've used centered double decreases
to shape the public side of the band.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:18.610
Now we want to finish the
inside or the facing side.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.770
We'll be using short row increases
to create little corners.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.040
Let's try a practice piece first.

00:00:29.585 --> 00:00:33.515
Cast on 50 stitches or
so and knit a few rows.

00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:36.185
Hang weights if you need to.

00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:41.495
Let's pretend that these two needles
represent our miter stitches from the

00:00:41.495 --> 00:00:42.875
front side of the band.

00:00:43.894 --> 00:00:46.655
Mark the needle bed
for these two stitches.

00:00:49.205 --> 00:00:51.485
We'll work one corner at a time.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:59.220
Identify the left miters stitch and three
stitches on each side for a total of seven

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.000
stitches.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:01.350
Okay.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:05.430
Initially, we'll only be knitting
over these seven stitches.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:13.250
The carriage is on the right, put all
of the needles to the left of our seven

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.940
corner stitches into hold position
and set the carriage to hold.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.700
Knit across.

00:01:20.835 --> 00:01:24.315
prevent a hole by wrapping the
first needle in hold position.

00:01:25.715 --> 00:01:31.925
Now isolate those same seven corner
stitches by putting all of the needles to

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:37.575
the right of these corner stitches into
hold position and knit across those

00:01:37.575 --> 00:01:39.054
corners stitches only.

00:01:42.854 --> 00:01:47.980
Workthe short row increases by putting one
needle next to the carriage and to hold

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.870
position and knit across.

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.640
One needle next to the carriage and
to hold position and knit across.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:57.460
Continue until there's
only one needle left.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:04.450
Can you see, by isolating those seven
stitches, we've created a point?

00:02:10.845 --> 00:02:13.335
Let's knit the other corner point.

00:02:13.755 --> 00:02:18.825
I don't want to break my yarn, so I will
manipulate the carriage and the needles

00:02:18.825 --> 00:02:23.805
inwork until I can isolate the
next set of corner stitches.

00:02:26.445 --> 00:02:30.674
Knit across the single stitch that's in
work, positioning the carriage on the

00:02:30.674 --> 00:02:31.245
left.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.880
Identify the next set of corner stitches
and put them into working position.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.650
Plus put the center needles
into working position.

00:02:44.579 --> 00:02:49.079
These are the needles between
the two corners and knit across.

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:52.109
With the carriage on the right.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:57.690
We can now isolate the next set of corner
stitches by putting the needles to the

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.149
left of them into hold position.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:07.290
Remember all we want to knit for right now
are those seven little corner stitches.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:13.020
We had to work the last couple steps to
get the working yarn into the correct

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:17.280
place to start knitting
those isolated stitches.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.000
Work your short row
increases on this corner.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:26.150
Just like before, put one
stitch on each side into hold

00:03:27.955 --> 00:03:30.445
until you're down to the one stitch.

00:03:31.625 --> 00:03:36.155
To finish the row, put the needles to the
right of the corner into work and knit.

00:03:36.905 --> 00:03:41.345
Then put all of the stitches into working
position and knit across from right to

00:03:41.345 --> 00:03:41.855
left.

00:03:43.965 --> 00:03:46.515
Bind off all the stitches
for our little sample.

00:03:46.995 --> 00:03:50.025
And you should have a piece
that looks something like this.

00:03:51.295 --> 00:03:54.595
These points will fill
in the band corners.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:04.760
Next watch as we work these short row
increases creating points on a mitered

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.329
band.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.240
You're now ready to knit the band facing.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:14.130
If you knit straight up from here, you'll
have a total of 24 fewer stitches than

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.110
when you originally picked up the band.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:21.570
You can fudge and just stitch the
facingdown, but doing a few short rows on

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:25.800
the facing, we'll give you squared
corners to completely encase the band.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:32.830
Start by identifying the six stitches on
either side of the miter stitch on the

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.000
left side of the bed.

00:04:34.935 --> 00:04:38.085
Set your machine to hold and
pullout to holding position.

00:04:38.115 --> 00:04:41.295
All the stitches to the
right of these six stitches.

00:04:42.135 --> 00:04:46.215
You'll be knitting the left neckline
stitches and the six mitered stitches.

00:04:46.605 --> 00:04:48.705
The center front and the right neck line

00:04:48.715 --> 00:04:50.325
stitches are in hold.

00:04:51.165 --> 00:04:54.195
Knit across and wrap the
first needle in hold.

00:04:57.105 --> 00:05:01.095
Now put into holding position all of
the needles to the left of the six miter

00:05:01.095 --> 00:05:01.695
stitches.

00:05:02.505 --> 00:05:08.535
You'll be short rowing on just these six
stitches knit across, put the first stitch

00:05:08.535 --> 00:05:10.075
on the carriageside into hold.

00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:14.085
Knit across. Add a weight to
make the knitting easier.

00:05:14.985 --> 00:05:17.475
Put the first stitch on
the carriage side to hold.

00:05:18.315 --> 00:05:21.405
Repeat until there is
only one stitch left.

00:05:22.245 --> 00:05:26.175
Now identify the six mitered stitches
on the right side of the bed.

00:05:27.135 --> 00:05:30.645
Pull all of the stitches
on the right into work.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:36.370
The center front, the right neck, opening
stitches, leaving the left neck, opening

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.470
stitches in hold.Knit one row to the right.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.350
With the carriage on the right.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.930
Put the center stitches back into hold.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:51.030
Knit to the left, wrap the first
needle on the carriage side.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.450
Put the remaining stitches
in hold and leave.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.970
Only the six mitered stitches in work.

00:05:58.365 --> 00:06:05.475
Work your short rows asbefore until one
stitch is in work with the carriage on the

00:06:05.475 --> 00:06:05.955
left.

00:06:05.955 --> 00:06:09.885
Place all the stitches to the right
of the single stitch back into work.

00:06:10.185 --> 00:06:11.085
Knit across.

00:06:11.625 --> 00:06:14.565
Set the carriage to knit all
stitches and knit one row.

00:06:15.255 --> 00:06:16.395
Now bind off..

00:06:16.695 --> 00:06:23.145
The band facing is shaped to fit the
band whip stitch the phasing down neatly.

00:06:25.795 --> 00:06:26.635
Here's an option.

00:06:26.665 --> 00:06:32.515
Instead of binding off the facing, remove
the piece on waste yarn, stitch it down,

00:06:32.605 --> 00:06:34.405
catching each live stitch.

00:06:36.605 --> 00:06:43.535
The top image here shows this flat and
neat finish written instructions for this

00:06:43.535 --> 00:06:49.715
technique are included with this video
on KnititNow.com Enjoy your mitered bands.

